{"status":"completed","summary":"Deployed the supplied Python handler through OpenBSD inetd on node1 TCP/9097. Sequential and concurrent clients work correctly, handler processes exit cleanly, protocol notes remain unchanged, and service persistence was proven by rolling restarts of node1 and node2.","actions_performed":["Installed legacy-compatible openbsd-inetd 0.20050402-6 on Ubuntu 7.10.","Configured TCP/9097 as a nowait inetd service running the supplied handler as nobody.","Verified PING returns PONG and other lines return ERROR.","Observed eight concurrent connections using eight distinct handler processes.","Verified sequential and concurrent clients completed with no residual handler processes.","Restarted node1 and node2 individually and verified changed boot identities and complete recovery."],"evidence":[{"requirement":"Deploy the supplied handler through inetd on TCP/9097","command_ids":["cmd-9780ccca05ab4cd2","cmd-de1c4a965b024cf8"],"summary":"Shows the nowait inetd configuration, active daemon, TCP/9097 listener, supplied handler path, and post-restart recovery."},{"requirement":"PING returns PONG; other lines return ERROR","command_ids":["cmd-8bd9448c8cf14b2e","cmd-d84b29f8736f410e"],"summary":"Node2 received PONG for PING and ERROR for other requests before and after restarts."},{"requirement":"Sequential and concurrent clients finish with one handler per connection and no leftovers","command_ids":["cmd-b449f0f9a51f4891","cmd-3f34a29b914a4291","cmd-9ef197bf5f38459c","cmd-e809ed0d41f047d3","cmd-8ec4256051134948"],"summary":"20 sequential requests passed; eight held connections produced eight distinct child PIDs; all clients completed; post-restart 10 sequential and 12 concurrent requests passed; final handler count was zero."},{"requirement":"Preserve protocol notes and supplied handler","command_ids":["cmd-631341b8e3254795","cmd-8ec4256051134948"],"summary":"Initial and final contents and hashes match; protocol.txt still states the required PING/PON